{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"little-untimely-grison","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_commands cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:1-13, 127-201, 247-281, 333-472, 586-674` — Preserve parsing distinctions, gate/cascade order, and unsigned-close signal. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:1-27, 80-157, 183-298, 416-479, 620-636` — Preserve lock scope, metadata schema, atomic claim, close-class validation, and non-codebase laundering guard. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py:1-39, 66-74, 250-256, 381-562` — Preserve enforcement scope, live-versus-ledger provenance, authentic-signature classification, and batched commit resolution. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py:1-23, 56-64, 164-197` — Preserve terminal event anchors, live fingerprint recomputation, trust-era checks, and fail-closed missing anchors. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"ab62-e1a6-df62-42fa","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar/_commands — cohort 03: transition–verify_opcert"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570712665497220,"uuid":"c929c2d9-4ddf-45a9-ac50-5dd0f2795de7"}